    "type": "question",
    "label": "23",
    "prompt": "The line $y=2x+1$ meets the parabola $y=x^2-3x-1$ in two points $P$ and $Q$. Find the midpoint of $P$ and $Q$ without solving for their coordinates.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\left(\\frac52,6\\right)$.",
      "worked": "Equate the line and parabola:\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+1&=x^2-3x-1\\\\x^2-5x-2&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nLet the intersection $x$-coordinates be $x_1$ and $x_2$. Their sum is $5$, so the midpoint has\n$$x_M=\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2}=\\frac52.$$\nThe midpoint lies on the line:\n$$y_M=2\\left(\\frac52\\right)+1=6.$$\nTherefore, the midpoint is $\\left(\\frac52,6\\right)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 78
  },
